SUMMARY:Maynard Institute's Fire Up Entrepreneurship Program
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260515T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260515T000000
UID:652e50cc5cb4a6deaee1b608de24f124@sej.org
DESCRIPTION:The Robert C. Maynard Institute for Journalism Education is la
 unching a pilot cohort to support journalism entrepreneurs as part of the 
 California Propel Local News Initiative\, an effort to strengthen the stat
 e’s multi-lingual media ecosystem\, ensuring long-term sustainability of
  local public service journalism for underserved localities. The Fire Up E
 ntrepreneur Program\, as part of the Propel Initiative\, will train up to 
 16 people representing eight news organizations in revenue\, audience\, pr
 oduct and community with a focus on ensuring sustainability. Participants 
 will work with experts in business\, audience strategy and other topics.\n
 For California-serving newsrooms. Deadline May 15.\n\nCategories: Californ
 ia\, Workshops and Fellowships\, Journalism & Media
URL:https://www.sej.org/calendar/deadline-maynard-institutes-fire-entrepre
 neurship-program
X-SOURCE:Society of Environmental Journalists
END:VEVENT
