BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Society of Professional Journalists": "http://cpj.org/USJANcrowds"}
X-SOURCE-ID:spj
X-SOURCE:Society of Professional Journalists
DTSTAMP:20170606T23231Z
UID:MZ1B23t3Mw-8221312781@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260519T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260519T143000
SUMMARY:Journalist safety in the US: Crowds, protests, and events
URL:http://cpj.org/USJANcrowds
DESCRIPTION:Local and international journalists are gearing up to cover multiple major events in the U.S. this year -- including the World Cup and midterm elections -- and may face heightened risks as a result. Join the U.S. Journalist Assistance Network for a free roundtable focused on best practices for interacting with police and federal law enforcement\, crossing borders amid increased screenings\, preparing for device searches or seizures\, knowing your rights in the context of arrest or detention\, and navigating crowd or police violence at matches and rallies. The roundtable will feature legal and safety experts from Freedom of the Press Foundation\, International Women’s Media Foundation\, Kuck Baxter LLC\, and Reporters Committee for Freedom of the Press??'and will be moderated by PEN America. 
LOCATION:
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Tiny News Members Only": "https://us06web.zoom.us/j/88089952275?pwd=YhlBR0xdjYVuqhbfYJabn3gYm7MOcr.1"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tiny_news_members_only
X-SOURCE:Tiny News Members Only
URL:https://us06web.zoom.us/j/88089952275?pwd=YhlBR0xdjYVuqhbfYJabn3gYm7MOcr.1
SUMMARY:The Power and Purpose of Community Listening
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T140000
DTSTAMP:20260515T025512Z
UID:5ej8bcsqm4t9grca90kpdvg2hd@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T130000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260513T170654Z
DESCRIPTION:<p dir="ltr">For small\, independent local newsrooms\, communi
 ty connection is the foundation of everything. But community listening tak
 es time and effort\, and most small news founders are already stretched th
 in. How do you make that investment count? How do you take what you hear a
 nd turn it into something that can support your work? </p><p dir="ltr">Th
 is interactive workshop offers a practical\, people-centered approach to c
 ommunity listening designed specifically for indie newsrooms with limited 
 bandwidth and big ambitions. We'll explore low-lift\, low-budget methods t
 hat fit the reality of your team and the needs of your community\, and we'
 ll focus on how to plan and document your listening work so it actually pa
 ys off.</p><p dir="ltr">We'll work through four core ideas:</p><ul><li dir
 ="ltr"><p dir="ltr"><b>Right-size your approach:</b> You can’t do everyt
 hing\, and that’s just fine. We'll explore community listening practices
  and help you think about which ones fit your team’s goals and capacity.
 </p></li><li dir="ltr"><b><p dir="ltr">Tell your story: Community listenin
 g gives you the opportunity to share your mission and your work with the c
 ommunity\, and to gather their feedback. We’ll talk about how to prepare
  for that opportunity. </p></b></li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr"><b>Create 
 a virtuous cycle:</b> Listening isn't a one-time event — it's an ongoing
  loop of listening\, reporting\, sharing\, and feedback that builds trust 
 over time and keeps your community coming back. We’ll share ways to brin
 g what you hear back into your newsroom. </p></li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="l
 tr"><b>Let your community make the case:</b> Your readers and community me
 mbers are your best advocates. We'll explore how to capture and use what y
 ou hear to make the case for supporting your work — in grant application
 s\, membership campaigns\, and beyond.</p></li></ul><p dir="ltr">You'll le
 ave with practical tools for asset-mapping\, community outreach\, and case
 -making that you can put to use right away.</p><br>Tiny News Collective is
  inviting you to a scheduled Zoom meeting.<br><br>Topic: The Power and Pur
 pose of Community Listening<br>Time: May 19\, 2026 04:00 PM Eastern Time (
 US and Canada)<br>Join Zoom Meeting<br><a href="https://us06web.zoom.us/j/
 88089952275?pwd=YhlBR0xdjYVuqhbfYJabn3gYm7MOcr.1">https://us06web.zoom.us/
 j/88089952275?pwd=YhlBR0xdjYVuqhbfYJabn3gYm7MOcr.1</a><br><br>Meeting chat
  link<br><a href="https://us06web.zoom.us/launch/jc/88089952275">https://u
 s06web.zoom.us/launch/jc/88089952275</a><br><br>Meeting ID: 880 8995 2275<
 br>Passcode: 990480<br><br>---<br><br>One tap mobile<br>+13052241968\,\,88
 089952275#\,\,\,\,*990480# US<br>+13017158592\,\,88089952275#\,\,\,\,*9904
 80# US (Washington DC)<br><br><br>---<br><br>Join by SIP<br>• 8808995227
 5@zoomcrc.com<br><br>Join instructions<br><a href="https://us06web.zoom.us
 /meetings/88089952275/invitations?signature=VeF9i8X5nssrZRqJb8dNUPIkx0h_g6
 VsuNyPx3zxT5Q">https://us06web.zoom.us/meetings/88089952275/invitations?si
 gnature=VeF9i8X5nssrZRqJb8dNUPIkx0h_g6VsuNyPx3zxT5Q</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260514T202713Z
LOCATION:https://us06web.zoom.us/j/88089952275?pwd=YhlBR0xdjYVuqhbfYJabn3g
 Ym7MOcr.1
